            "commit_id": "c179c25c57beb00f1f9ecdaa7fceb14ba26c868d",
            "created_at": "2026-07-30T05:20:19Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -189,11 +189,18 @@ If your terminal emulator responds with >\n         CSI ? <flags> u\n this means your terminal supports the \"CSI u\" encoding and Nvim will tell your\n terminal to enable it by writing the sequence >\n-        CSI > 1 u\n+        CSI > 3 u\n If your terminal does not support \"CSI u\" then Nvim will instead enable the\n \"modifyOtherKeys\" encoding by writing the sequence >\n         CSI > 4 ; 2 m\n \n+The \"3\" is a set of kitty keyboard protocol \"progressive enhancement\" flags:",
